  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through Sunday)\nIssued at 137 AM CDT Mon Jul 27 2026\n\nThe effects of upper level high pressure continue in the extended \nperiod. The main idea for the rest of the week and next weekend \nstill comprise of a slight and gradual decrease in high temperatures \nwith favorable rain chances confined largely in the northwest \ncombined Panhandles.\n\nAs the upper ridge steadily shifts west and heights decrease, \nmaximum temperatures will retrograde from mid 100s to lower 100s and \neventually upper 90s heading into the weekend. That said, some local \nhot spots in our CWA will are still expected to hold onto triple \ndigit heat throughout the long term period. Locations like Palo Duro \nCanyon, Boys Ranch, and Borger (towns near the Canadian River \nValley) have a high chance to achieve high temperatures greater than \n100 degrees for more than 15 consecutive days.\n\nIsolated to scattered showers are still forecast to affect the \nnorthwest combined Panhandles this week due to our northwest flow \nregime. There may be a couple of days where PoPs expand further \nsouth and east, but that will depend on potential shortwaves or \noutflow, alongside minimal inhibition, to regenerate convection \nfurther into our CWA.\n\nRangel",
